{
  "id": "fMQ15943GzYcH6bw",
  "name": "WF-02 Incident Intelligence",
  "description": "Onward Phase 3: interprets a persisted incident using trusted asset context (registered asset + prior incidents for it) and, if the incident has a media_url, real image evidence. Calls decision-engine's /incident/interpret — the only place the model call lives, Groq by default; the provider is swappable via decision-engine's MODEL_PROVIDER env var and never touches this workflow — then persists the result to incident_intelligence, separate from the user's original report. Idempotent — skips re-interpretation if intelligence already exists.",
  "active": true,
  "note": "Published and live-gate-tested (Phase 3, third pass — image intake; Phase 4 pass — impact trigger + a real defect fix). Bugs found and fixed: (1) Phase 3 — Has Media?/Fetch Image/Encode Image lacked executeOnce and ran once per item from Fetch Prior Incidents (up to 5x) instead of once — fixed with executeOnce:true on 'Has Media?' alone; (2) Phase 3 — {{ $binary.data.data }} does not resolve to base64 in this instance's filesystem-v2 binary storage mode — replaced with the dedicated Extract from File node; (3) Phase 4, found live during the Phase 4 gate — 'Fetch Prior Incidents' had no alwaysOutputData, so the FIRST-EVER incident for any asset (0 prior rows) made it emit 0 items, which silently skipped every downstream node (Call Decision Engine, Insert Intelligence, Trigger Impact never ran) even though the execution reported \"success\". Fixed with alwaysOutputData:true on 'Fetch Prior Incidents' plus a `.filter(i => i.json.description)` guard on the prior_incidents mapping in Call Decision Engine's jsonBody, so the synthetic {} placeholder item never turns into a bogus prior-incident record. Verified live against HVAC-12's first-ever incident. 'Call Decision Engine' URL points at a Cloudflare Quick Tunnel (*.trycloudflare.com) — ephemeral, must be updated whenever the tunnel restarts. Phase 4 addition, published and live: a 'Trigger Impact' node fires WF-03 Operational Impact fire-and-forget from Insert Intelligence's success output, mirroring WF-01's existing Trigger Intelligence pattern exactly. Phase 5 gate note: a real Phase 5 live-gate run exposed that Groq's required_capability output is free-form prose (e.g. 'Level 1 Inspection (Power/Connections)'), never matching any real technician/inventory tag downstream — fixed with a deterministic vocabulary clamp in decision-engine (app/schemas/incident.py's apply_review_policy normalizes any out-of-vocabulary value to GENERAL_MAINTENANCE and forces review), since Groq's own JSON-schema enum constraint proved unreliable for this model. This workflow itself required no changes for that fix. Hardening checkpoint: 'Call Decision Engine' URL updated to the current Cloudflare Quick Tunnel after runtime cleanup (old tunnel process torn down, exactly one new one started). Added retryOnFail (3 tries, 1s wait) to Fetch Incident, Check Existing Intelligence, Fetch Asset, Fetch Prior Incidents, and Insert Intelligence -- Insert Intelligence is safe to retry because incident_intelligence.incident_id is a PRIMARY KEY, so a retry-after-actual-duplicate hits the existing constraint and falls through to the existing onError branch, never creating a second row (live node settings not re-serialized here in full; n8n is canonical per CLAUDE.md §9).",
  "settings": { "executionOrder": "v1", "availableInMCP": true },
  "nodes": [
    { "id": "798123d5-4ddb-4047-a633-94ec8b76557d", "name": "Intelligence Trigger", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger", "typeVersion": 1.2, "position": [200, 400], "parameters": { "inputSource": "workflowInputs", "workflowInputs": { "values": [{ "name": "incident_id", "type": "string" }] } } },
    { "id": "903d59e3-aec8-442a-884e-940defcd31e0", "name": "Fetch Incident", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.supabase", "typeVersion": 1, "position": [420, 400], "alwaysOutputData": true, "parameters": { "resource": "row", "operation": "getAll", "tableId": "incidents", "returnAll": false, "limit": 1, "filterType": "manual", "matchType": "allFilters", "filters": { "conditions": [{ "keyName": "id", "condition": "eq", "keyValue": "={{ $json.incident_id }}" }] } }, "credentials": { "supabaseApi": { "id": "dYRlahdtvOfzgkpw", "name": "Supabase (Onward)" } } },
    { "id": "c0517924-2808-4a6d-8dc2-59e5ebd43e68", "name": "Incident Found?", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if", "typeVersion": 2.2, "position": [640, 400], "parameters": { "conditions": { "options": { "caseSensitive": true, "leftValue": "", "typeValidation": "strict" }, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{ "leftValue": "={{ $json.id }}", "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "notEmpty" }, "rightValue": "" }] } } },
